      "startLine": 21,
      "code": "\n    /**\n     * The delay before the given attempt: the base doubled {@code attempt} times, stopping at the cap. The first\n     * attempt (zero) waits the base, and so does any earlier one.\n     */\n    public long delayMillis(int attempt) {\n        long delay = baseMillis;\n        for (int i = 0; i < attempt && delay < capMillis; i++) {\n            delay = Math.min(capMillis, delay * 2);\n        }\n        return delay;\n    }\n}\n"
    },
    "after": {
      "file": "examples/apps/crosscut/src/main/java/net/terminalvalue/crosscut/retry/Backoff.java",
      "startLine": 21,
      "code": "\n    /**\n     * The delay before the given attempt: the base doubled {@code attempt} times, stopping at the cap. The first\n     * attempt (zero) waits the base, and so does any earlier one. Doubling {@code attempt} times is a shift, kept\n     * short of the sign bit: a shift that would leave the range of a {@code long} is already past the cap.\n     */\n    public long delayMillis(int attempt) {\n        if (attempt <= 0) {\n            return baseMillis;\n        }\n        int shift = Math.min(attempt, Long.numberOfLeadingZeros(baseMillis) - 1);\n        return Math.min(capMillis, baseMillis << shift);\n    }\n}\n"
    },
